        socket_bind($this->socket, $host, $port);
        socket_listen($this->socket);
    public function handle($client) {
        $data = 'Hello from your side';
        send($client, $data);
        return true;
    }
}

Client side:
$client = socket_accept($socket);
$data = 'Connection accepted';
$client->send($data);
socket_close($client);

How to Protect:
Update your web server to drop the SYN flags, adjust firewall rules to filter out SYN packets, and ensure your database locks prevent concurrent writes on the same connection during a high-volume SYN flood.

